<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">23032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The <sub alias="International Energy Agency">IEA</sub>'s called the closure of the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> the equivalent of the nineteen-seventies oil shock and Russia's twenty twenty-two gas cutoff combined.</s> <s>Brent crude's topped a hundred and fourteen dollars as Asian markets plunged — Tokyo's Nikkei fell four percent, and the French oil major TotalEnergies warned a six-month war would exhaust global reserves that cover just three to four months.</s> <s>Trump's forty-eight-hour ultimatum to reopen the strait expires tonight... and Iran has pledged to close it completely if its power plants are struck.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israeli forces have entered southern Lebanon, opening a third front in a war that's killed more than a thousand Lebanese and displaced a million in eighteen days.</s> <s>Airstrikes systematically targeted bridges and medical facilities before the ground advance — the first Israeli incursion into Lebanese territory since two thousand and six.</s> <s>Whether this becomes an occupation or a limited operation depends on how Hezbollah responds in the coming days.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>US-Israeli airstrikes cut power to the western Iranian city of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɒrəmɑːˈbɑːd">Khorramabad</phoneme> overnight, expanding the bombing campaign from military targets to civilian electricity infrastructure.</s> <s>Disabling power grids to break public morale follows the same playbook used in Iraq in ninety-one and Yugoslavia in ninety-nine.</s> <s>The expansion to civilian targets raises the question of whether Iran will retaliate beyond the strait.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Libya's grand mufti has declared supporting Iran a religious duty — the first such ruling from a national religious authority since the war began.</s> <s>Most Muslim-majority governments have either backed the US-Israeli campaign or stayed silent, making al-Ghariani's declaration a direct challenge to that consensus.</s> <s>Saudi state clerics now face the task of reconciling his ruling with Riyadh's alignment with Washington.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Four Ukrainians died as Russian forces claimed a village in the Sumy region, advancing under improved spring weather while the Iran crisis absorbs NATO's diplomatic bandwidth.</s> <s>Moscow's stated aim is a permanent buffer zone in Sumy, stretching Ukraine's defenses across a second major front hundreds of kilometers from the Donbas line.</s> <s>The offensive's received almost no international attention this week.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Slovenia rationed fuel on election day after cross-border drivers stripped stations dry, exploiting open Schengen borders as war-driven hoarding spread across central Europe.</s> <s>The government deployed the army to restore supply and opened a criminal inquiry into price manipulation.</s> <s>It's the first military fuel deployment in a Schengen country since the bloc was founded.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An explosion collapsed two buildings in Istanbul's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fɑːˈtiː">Fatih</phoneme> district, killing one person.</s> <s>Three years after earthquakes killed fifty thousand across Turkey, the building inspection overhaul still hasn't reached older neighborhoods built before seismic codes existed.</s> <s>Prosecutors are investigating structural failure after the gas utility found no evidence of a leak.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's rupee hit a record low as oil crossed a hundred and twelve dollars — a direct consequence of importing eighty-five percent of its crude.</s> <s>Each ten-dollar rise in oil adds fifteen billion dollars to the current account deficit, a structural vulnerability that no central bank intervention can fix.</s> <s>The Reserve Bank is burning through foreign reserves to defend the currency while markets wait for ceasefire talks that haven't materialized.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's diesel price has tripled since the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> closed.</s> <s>Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif told two hundred and forty million Pakistanis to work from home and avoid travel, creating a twenty-seven-billion-rupee austerity fund to absorb the shock.</s> <s>The country now waits to see whether Saudi Arabia can reroute enough crude around the closed strait to prevent outright shortages.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Malaysia spends two billion ringgit a month holding fuel prices steady, absorbing every cent of the fifty-percent post-war crude rise through public finances.</s> <s>Brent at a hundred and twelve dollars already exceeds the hundred-dollar threshold the deputy prime minister named as the country's breaking point.</s> <s>How long the treasury can sustain this is now Malaysia's central fiscal question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Gold has fallen for nine consecutive trading days, sliding to four thousand three hundred and sixty dollars even as wars rage on three fronts.</s> <s>War-driven inflation has pushed central banks toward rate rises, making gold's zero yield a liability rather than a refuge.</s> <s>Sovereign wealth funds are liquidating holdings for cash — breaking the centuries-old assumption that gold is where money goes when the world burns.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The <sub alias="World Meteorological Organization">WMO</sub> has confirmed twenty twenty-five as the hottest year in recorded history, with ocean warming doubling in rate since two thousand and five.</s> <s>Chief Celeste Saulo said the heat is now permanently locked into the climate system — even if emissions stopped tomorrow, the warming already absorbed would persist for thousands of years.</s> <s>The only question left is how much worse it gets, God willing not as bad as the models suggest.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Chinese surgical robot outperformed human surgeons by twenty-nine percent in brain angiography — a procedure that requires threading a guide wire from the thigh to the brain under X-ray.</s> <s>The finding matters less for speed than for safety: surgeons accumulate radiation damage over entire careers from these procedures, and the robot eliminates that exposure entirely.</s> <s>Study authors called the results preliminary, but the radiation argument may prove harder to dismiss than the precision one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Former FDA Commissioner Robert Califf warned that politics now drives US drug approvals.</s> <s>Dozens of countries treat FDA decisions as their reference standard, so political interference in Washington ripples directly into drug safety from Lagos to Jakarta.</s> <s>Patients waiting for rare-disease gene therapies now depend on an approval process shaped more by political calculation than clinical evidence.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Entry-level jobs are vanishing as a new generation starts their careers, with AI tools now handling writing, coding, and analysis at scale before positions are formally cut.</s> <s>Graduates can see the roles they trained for being automated in real time — a form of displacement that's visible years before it shows up in unemployment statistics.</s> <s>Whether AI-resistant career paths outlast the next wave of automation is the generation-defining bet these workers are making with their lives.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea's POSCO is breaking China's near-total monopoly on rare earth magnets essential for electric vehicle motors.</s> <s>Dysprosium and terbium — critical for EV drivetrains — are produced almost entirely in China, giving Beijing leverage over the entire global supply chain.</s> <s>POSCO's US processing plant opens in twenty twenty-seven, marking the first serious industrial challenge to that dominance.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>